-- הסכם עוז לתמורה (14.8.2011), §62: employing a teaching employee in a work
-- week with 9-hour days is conditional on the Minister of Industry, Trade
-- and Labour approving the agreement for a 9-hour day under §5 of the Hours
-- of Work and Rest Law, 1951; without the approval, the reform's week is
-- adjusted, by agreement, so that no day is longer than the law's.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT `oz-founding-common`
IMPORT `oz-founding-9`
IMPORT hours_of_work_law

§ `62`

DECLARE `Oz section 62 action` IS ONE OF
    `adjust the reform's work week so no day exceeds the law's working day`

-- ¶1: the agreement's week has days of 9 hours: §9(ב)'s long day of 8:00
-- to 16:00, with §9(ד)'s hour from 16:00 to 17:00. Employing a teacher in
-- it depends on the Minister's approval of the agreement for a 9-hour day,
-- under §5 of the Hours of Work and Rest Law ("החוק"). Without it, the
-- week of the reform in full is adjusted, by agreement (no day set:
-- convention dates.no-deadline), so that the day is no longer than the
-- law's working day (§2 of the Hours of Work and Rest Law, imported).
@ref akn:art_62/p1
`the working day section 62 speaks of` MEANS 9

`the longest Oz working day` MEANS `the length of the Oz working day` `a long working day` PLUS 1

GIVEN `the Minister approved a 9-hour day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 9-hour working day may be worked under section 62` `the Minister approved a 9-hour day` IF
    `the Minister approved a 9-hour day`

GIVEN `the Minister approved a 9-hour day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law's working day` IS A NUMBER @desc in hours, as the Hours of Work and Rest Law defines it
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the longest working day section 62 allows` `the Minister approved a 9-hour day` `the law's working day` IS
    IF `a 9-hour working day may be worked under section 62` `the Minister approved a 9-hour day`
    THEN `the working day section 62 speaks of`
    ELSE `the law's working day`

GIVEN `the Minister approved a 9-hour day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Oz section 62 action`
DECIDE `adjusting the week without the approval` `the Minister approved a 9-hour day` IS
    IF `the Minister approved a 9-hour day`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE (PARTY `the employer`
          MUST  `adjust the reform's work week so no day exceeds the law's working day`)
         RAND
         (PARTY `the secondary teachers' organisation`
          MUST  `adjust the reform's work week so no day exceeds the law's working day`)

-- The Hours of Work and Rest Law (imported): without the approval the
-- day is §2's, eight hours, which §5 keeps unless the Minister approved the
-- agreement's day; with it, nine, no longer than the two long days §5(ב)
-- lets an approved agreement set. Either way the day is the law's: the
-- floor is met.
`section 62 keeps the Oz day within the Hours of Work and Rest Law` MEANS
        `the longest working day section 62 allows` FALSE (`the longest working day section 2 allows` FALSE)
            EQUALS `the working day the law counts` FALSE `the working day section 62 speaks of` FALSE
    AND `the longest working day section 62 allows` TRUE (`the longest working day section 2 allows` FALSE)
            AT MOST `the long day section 5(ב) lets an approved agreement set`
#ASSERT `section 62 keeps the Oz day within the Hours of Work and Rest Law`

§§ `62 -- illustrations`

-- the 9-hour day is §9's long day with (ד)'s completing hour
#ASSERT `the longest Oz working day` EQUALS `the working day section 62 speaks of`
#ASSERT `the longest working day section 62 allows` TRUE 8 EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `the longest working day section 62 allows` FALSE 8 EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `adjusting the week without the approval` TRUE EQUALS FULFILLED
